# Cluster scripts run on Linux — CRLF in .sh/.sbatch fails silently there.
cluster/** text eol=lf
dataset_cache/**/*.pkl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
dataset_cache/**/*.pkl.part-* filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pdf binary

# A frozen protocol snapshot is a hashed artifact, not editable source. Its
# SHA-256 is recorded inside the runs that were gated on it, so a checkout that
# rewrites its line endings silently changes its identity: on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true) the LF blob lands as CRLF and hashes to something the
# gate cannot recognise. Marking it binary makes the checkout byte-exact
# everywhere, which is the only form in which the hash means anything.
docs/experiments/*.frozen-*.md -text
